A decision for the maintainer (found under k327, apply worker, 2026-10-31): should a control plane that is still not Ready after the first deploy's 600 s wait end `ocp apply` APPLY INCOMPLETE (non-zero exit), or WITH WARNINGS, or go on as today (STDERR line since k327, run continues, exit 0)?

ADR 0017 does not settle it: its principle (the banner is a statement about the cluster) points to failing; its pod scan takes Pending as "still starting" (an accepted consequence); its amendment handles node readiness case by case and provisionally (AMD: a failed component; NVIDIA: a warning, open on k285). In code, k226 already counts police2+ and workers that are not Ready as failed components -- only the first control plane is not.

Related: k285 (an NVIDIA node without nvidia.com/gpu allocatable: failed component?). Both are the same question -- what node-level readiness counts as failure -- and could be decided together, then recorded as an ADR 0017 amendment.

Maintainer's decision 2026-11-06 (hub perl-developer-bb, kubernetes-ocp-entscheidungen.md, e0ba4b5): a first control plane that is not Ready after the first deploy's wait is a failed component: apply ends APPLY INCOMPLETE with a non-zero exit, as for police2+ and workers today. An ADR 0017 amendment records the rule for all nodes: a node that never got Ready is a failure, and so is an NVIDIA or AMD node without allocatable GPU.

Done per the maintainer's 2026-11-06 decision (apply worker + adr auditor). Bootstrap.pm ~693-720: a first control plane not seen Ready within the 600 s wait is a failed component; its STDERR line is now a counted-failure line (it was a WARN) and still carries the Ready condition or the failed read; counted as control plane NAME, the name unready_nodes gives police2+, so Health::finish ends APPLY INCOMPLETE, exit 1. The run goes on as after a police2+ that did not join; on a node that stays NotReady the registry step still dies first, non-zero with no banner, as before. t/327 new subtest (counted, exit 1, banner; Ready / Ready within the wait / failed connectivity check count nothing), tag claims in t/327 and t/319. Red on 585cc31 with %INC asserted: t/327 4 of 6 subtests fail, t/319 1 of 4. Binding make test rel1106-pins 11 files / 124 tests PASS. ADR 0017 amendment 2026-11-06 records the rule for all nodes (first CP, police2+, workers, NVIDIA and AMD allocatable) and the reconcile gap as open on k417; inline markers and a README provenance paragraph.

